     ["A seventh failure mode, and the first where the pattern's own canonical number is the casualty. Prior modes: the method absent (L4), the site real but misplaced (slice 1), the output de-typed at the boundary (slice 2), every obligation discharged by the wrong lane (slice 3), the method correct but wired to the wrong verdict (slice 4), the clause satisfied by the method's absence (slice 5), the method flown once and never entered into the corpus (slice 6). Here the method IS the gate the source names, the gate IS built, and it passes the one measurement it existed to protect. The attestation's cited clause reads 'Mask-in still requires the null be CLEAN: settled, two distinct-as-of scans agreeing within epsilon; a confounded null discriminates nothing.' `validity-mask` (flight_record.clj:241-266) is that mask; it returned :in for live-df706c45 (checkpoint 13, 're-verifies CONFORMS with mask IN'; checkpoint 15, the :null stratum at n=1); and its window conjunct reads two scans and an ordering, never a duration."
      "The two canonical contrast cases differ 11.2-fold in the one dimension the method is about, and the mask cannot see the difference. live-957a4836, the CONTINUITY-POINT flight that discriminates 0x: begin 09:57:20Z, commit 09:57:38Z -- 18 seconds. live-df706c45, the OFF-CONTINUITY null that discriminates ~517x and is the reason the pattern exists: begin 10:21:59.505556758Z, commit 10:25:21Z -- 201.5 seconds. Same morning, same pilot, same apparatus. The pattern presents these two as the contrast in model-discrimination; they are also, unremarked, the contrast in window discipline, and in the opposite direction -- the flight whose number the pattern rests on is the one flown loose. The site is not concealing it: checkpoint 13 records 'the loose begin window (3.4 min, a file-race re-prep) was flagged in the record's own window-ground'. It flags and does not gate."
      "The field the mission says makes the confound checkable was nil on the flight it was introduced for. Checkpoint 11 added :begin-at and :scan-as-of to begin-live-cycle! because 'the stale-begin confound is checkable only if these are data'; checkpoint 12 is the first live use of that path; checkpoint 13 says the loose begin 'is checkable from :begin-at -- the confound is data now, not a story'. In the record: :begin-at is present and :scan-as-of is nil (organ/begin-state), because the pilot writes `(some-> (:as-of j) str)` (war_machine_pilot.clj:383) and the begin judgement carried no :as-of. And :begin-at is read by nothing -- `grep -rn begin-at src scripts test` over futon3c returns two writes, one pretty-printer that prints the string (flight_scope_view.bb:109) and two fixtures. Slice 3 recorded :scan-as-of as stored-and-unread from the other side of the same method; this slice adds that on the one flight where the confound was real, one of the two fields was never populated and the other has no reader."
      "The experiment was run twice and the first run's validity caveat was never answered or carried forward. PILOTS-LOG Turn 8 (2026-06-11, :194) flew the same shape a day before Turn 23 -- below-cap ohc 4, off the continuity point, a flat/null pair, predicted -4.1239 scaled vs realised -4.124 (error 6e-5), predicted-constant -4.0843 off by 0.04, 'scaled matches, constant misses' -- and flagged a CAVEAT 'to ground control as a QUESTION': it 'may not be a genuine model-test' because 'realised IS the field G which composes the same scaled predict-effects the model predicts with', so predicted==realised may be prior==value persisting through the target-sensitive fix. 'Needs source-check of whether realised has an observational component.' A grep for that text over futon3c holes/, src/ and scripts/ returns exactly the line that raised it. The pattern was minted on the repeat of an experiment whose own pilot had asked, and not been told, whether it measures anything external."
      "Third citation shape in the eight, and the first that can be held to anything. L4 and slices 1, 2, 4, 5 found :cited pointing at a NEXT-STEPS or cross-link line; slices 3 and 6 found it quoting the source's own THEN. Here it is a how-to-apply sentence, and unlike the other two shapes it states a gate condition naming a mechanism, so the site could in principle satisfy or fail it -- and does fail it. The running count across eight is now five NEXT-STEPS lines, two self-quoting THENs, one gate condition. Still no attestation in the set has cited a site."
      "The composition question the row could only ask at this slice has an answer, and it is not additive. Slice 3 established structurally that this method's baseline half is not carried out at this site and only its readback half is. Slice 6 established that this method's SOURCE was flown once and its result never entered the corpus. Composed, they predict exactly what slice 7 found in data: the one flight is the one where the missing half mattered, and the surviving half (settled readback, two scans past threshold agreeing within epsilon -- carried out correctly on this flight) is what let it through the gate. A half-implemented method does not fail loudly; it certifies the case it cannot see."]
